New case process:

* DETAILS View (three bars icon)

** Verify product is correct based on description (ImageManager for replication, Shadow Protect for backups, etc.)
*** All Restore issues for any product <mark>that do not mention testing or lab</mark> are immediately upgraded to Emergency Status:
**** Update Category Field. Include the Prefix "Restore - " (e.g. Restore - SPX - unable boot after restore)
**** Change the Priority to "Emergency"
**** Change the Owner to queue Emergency
**** Notify Team Lead that a case has been upgraded

** Verify required data has been provided for the product specified
*** ShadowProtect/SPX
**** Verify that DTX has been provided
**** Open them and verify the Serial Number from the Case matches the Product Key from the dtx.log located in C:\ProgramData\dtx\logs in the .7z file
**** Verify if this is an OEM License (OEM Support Contacts)
***** If OEM License, verify that Email Domain matches the OEM
***** If Email Domain does not match OEM, direct Partner to OEM for support
***** Valid Incident Packs holders are entitled to STC support.
**** Verify that the Serial Number has active maintenance in CPP
***** If Serial Number is expired, is there an Incident Pack referenced in the Web Form Incident field (e.g. XXXX-XXXX)
***** Verify that the Incident Pack is valid in CPP

